y of checkout-api v2.3.1 to production, the service failed health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west (error rate about 18%). The v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy in staging. checkout-api was rolled back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before it is redeployed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 50945, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01FBBr3TiLtc9aCf8QH8rhhp", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 50945, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01FBBr3TiLtc9aCf8QH8rhhp", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58012, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01TfddDtDmUq8crWe8M2y4xK", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {"confidence": 0.95}, "confidence": 0.95}, {"t_ms": 58312, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01TfddDtDmUq8crWe8M2y4xK", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58312, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01TfddDtDmUq8crWe8M2y4xK", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 68441, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's now passing health checks. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n1. **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy in staging.\n2. **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. All three regions now run it, and the error rate has dropped to about 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api). It describes the failure, the rollback and how the service is doing now. It also notes that the cause of the v2.3.1 problem needs to be found before it's redeployed. Opening the incident pages the on-call engineer.\n   - The request to create the incident timed out, so I checked the incident list before trying again. The incident had been created, so there's only one.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01A6XkufpHz5t23CSdSkRrkL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01T1KmDLE5mHC5zBy5LY6r7Y", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_014c1pTZ8mVZtHyDRRurFwWk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Ta876wECyn9AXr3bTyYW7q", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PTvHYAAZzMa9Usio8KZLN2", "caller": {"type": "direct"},